# Migrate Backend → Firebase Cloud Functions

Firebase project: **`dailyplanet-72e33`**

The existing `backend/` (Express server) will be replaced by a `functions/` folder that Firebase deploys directly to the cloud. The news and weather logic stays the same — only the wrapper changes.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Firebase Cloud Functions requires the **Blaze (pay-as-you-go) plan** to call external APIs (NewsAPI, OpenWeatherMap). You must upgrade at:
> **Firebase Console → Project Settings → Usage and billing → Modify plan → Blaze**
>
> Set a budget alert at $1 so you're notified before any real charges. With personal usage, cost will be $0.

## Proposed Changes

### Firebase Functions

#### [NEW] `functions/package.json`
Standard Firebase Functions Node.js project config with `axios`, `node-cache`, `firebase-functions`, `firebase-admin`.

#### [NEW] `functions/index.js`
Exports two HTTPS callable/onRequest functions:
- `news` → handles `/headlines?category=` and `/search?q=`
- `weather` → handles `?lat=&lon=`

#### [NEW] `functions/services/newsService.js`
Identical logic to current [backend/src/services/newsService.js](file:///c:/Users/shaah/OneDrive/Desktop/daily_planet/backend/src/services/newsService.js) — calls NewsAPI with 5-min cache.

#### [NEW] `functions/services/weatherService.js`
Identical logic to current [backend/src/services/weatherService.js](file:///c:/Users/shaah/OneDrive/Desktop/daily_planet/backend/src/services/weatherService.js) — calls OpenWeatherMap with 10-min cache.

#### [NEW] `functions/.gitignore`
Ignores `node_modules/`.

